libflui -- the FreeLFS desktop toolkit
======================================

Shared library, header (flui.h) and pkg-config file (flui.pc). C17, MIT.
flpanel, flterm, flsetup, flsettings, flfiles, fledit and flgreet-ui are built
on it. fl_app_mods() gives the modifiers held right now (ui->mods is only as
fresh as the last key press).

What is in it
  gfx.c   canvas, rectangles, anti-aliased paths (own scanline rasteriser,
          SVG path data) and the built-in icons (paths from the mockups; file,
          document, drive, home, trash, mute, ethernet, up, plus and three
          24-unit large ones for the file manager were added later)
  text.c  fontconfig + FreeType + HarfBuzz, glyph cache, fallback fonts;
          light hinting, whole-pixel advances
  conf.c  theme tokens (dark, light), the accent colour (accent= in desktop.conf: green,
          teal, blue, amber, orange, rose or RRGGBB; fl_accents, fl_accent_find; on_accent
          and the selection fill are derived) and ~/.config/freelfs/desktop.conf with an
          inotify watcher: apps that call fl_app_watch_conf pick up a theme or accent
          change live
  wl.c    Wayland client: windows (xdg toplevel with client-side title bar,
          or bare surfaces for the panel), wl_shm buffers, pointer, keyboard
          (xkbcommon, key repeat, dead keys), clipboard (wl_data_device),
          poll loop with fds and timers
  ui.c    widgets: label, button, icon button, text field, switch, scrollbar,
          list, grid helper, title bar; Tab focus
  kbd.c   the four keyboard layouts, keyboard.conf, tiles and key preview
  worldmap.c, worldmap_data.c
          time zones (tzdata's zone.tab, fl_tz_*), a flat world map widget
          (fl_worldmap_draw: Natural Earth projection, nearest-place regions, pins,
          hover cards) and a city search field with a suggestion list
          (fl_tzsearch_*); the installer uses the same widgets

Model: immediate mode. A window has a draw callback; each input event runs it
once, and widget calls draw and return what the user did. Idle means no work:
the loop blocks in poll(2). A pass redraws the whole (small) window into a
free wl_shm buffer; if the compositor still holds both, the pass runs dry
(input is handled, nothing drawn) and the picture follows on release.

Environment
  FLUI_PPM=FILE        no compositor: render the first frame of each window
                       to FILE (FILE.1, FILE.2 for further windows) as PPM
  FLUI_PPM_DELAY=MS    let fds and timers run that long before rendering
  FLUI_CONF=FILE       desktop.conf path
  FL_KEYBOARD_CONF=F   keyboard.conf path (default /etc/keyboard.conf)

Fonts: IBM Plex Sans (UI, 13 px) and Plex Mono, package ibm-plex.

Build: make; make install (PREFIX, LIBDIR, DESTDIR). Needs wayland-client,
freetype2, harfbuzz, fontconfig, xkbcommon and wayland-protocols at build time.

World map data: worldmap_data.c is generated by tools/mkworldmap.py (python3 -I, standard
library only) from Natural Earth 4.1.0 1:110m land and admin-0 countries (shared borders
only), simplified to 0.06 degrees and stored as int16 in 0.05 degree units (70 kB).
Source: https://naciscdn.org/naturalearth/110m/physical/ne_110m_land.zip and
.../cultural/ne_110m_admin_0_countries.zip. Natural Earth is public domain (no permission
needed, no attribution required; https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/).
To regenerate: python3 -I tools/mkworldmap.py ne_110m_land.shp ne_110m_admin_0_countries.shp > worldmap_data.c
FL_ZONEINFO (zoneinfo directory), FL_TZ_ETC (where /etc/timezone is read) and FL_NOW (a fixed
time) are test hooks of the time zone functions.
